  "text": "Species that have branched out from a single ancestor and adapted to many different habitats often appear on isolated land masses where newcomers encounter little competition. We looked at whether famous examples of such diversification among small perching birds on these isolated areas have generated unusually high variation in body shape compared with similarly aged groups elsewhere in the world. To test this, we recorded eight different body dimensions for each species and used these data to assess overall morphological disparity. Our analysis shows that the island groups display a level of shape diversity that exceeds that of comparable continental lineages, indicating that the unique ecological opportunities on isolated habitats can drive exceptional physical variation."
